    "id": "l1_coarse_pfree_tame_tail_distance_upgrade",
    "title": "L1 coarse p-free tame-tail distance upgrade",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For disjoint nonempty t-set locators F_X,F_Y in characteristic p, if t<p then their nonzero Wronskian W=F_X'F_Y-F_XF_Y' has degree at least t-1. Otherwise its Laurent expansion forces equality of the first t moments, and Newton identities identify the tails. Combining this lower degree with the coarse p-free upper degree gives t>=max(ceil((d+2)/2),min(d+1,p)) in every depth-d collision. Thus d<p has the full-prefix distance d+1, while every official checkpoint-depth collision has t>=p>n/24. The strict endpoint is sharp: an F_5 pair attains t=d+1 and deg W=t-1, while the F_4 t=p fixture refutes replacing t<p by t<=p. This proves no surviving exchange-subset bound or row-sharp Q.",
